*****************************************************************************
*
** Released by: Texas Instruments Inc.
* Part: TPS544B28 / TPS544A28 / TPS544B26 / TPS544A26 / TPS544628
* Date: 19NOV2026
* Model Type: TRANSIENT
* Simulator: PSPICE
* Simulator Version: 17.4 or later (last run on 23.1.0)
* EVM Order Number: TPS544B28EVM  [confirm EVM part # for A/26 variants]
* EVM Users Guide: SLVUD08
* Datasheet: SLVSHP8A (TPS544B28), SLVSHZ5 (TPS544628)
* Topologies Supported: Buck
*
* Model Version: 1.10
*
*****************************************************************************
*
* Updates:
*
* 1.10
* Added TPS544628 (6A, SLVSHZ5): set TPS544628=1 on TPS544B2x_TRANS (testbench PARAM
* part). Valley OCL default 7A (settings 4/5/6/7A, higher values clip to 7A), NOCL 3A,
* RDS(on) HS/LS 18m/7.5m. TPS544628=0 keeps the 1.00 behavior. Symbol unchanged.
*
* 1.00
* Release to Web.
*
*****************************************************************************
*
* Subcircuits provided (identical pinout, per-part defaults):
*   TPS544B28  - 20A grade, PMBus  (OCL default 21A)
*   TPS544A28  - 12A grade, PMBus  (OCL default 13A)
*   TPS544B26  - 20A grade, I2C   (OCL default 21A)
*   TPS544A26  - 12A grade, I2C   (OCL default 13A)
*   TPS544628  - 6A, PMBus: TPS544B2x_TRANS with TPS544628=1 (OCL default 7A)
* The digital interface (PMBus/I2C, pins ADR/SDA/SCL/MS1/MS2) is not
* modeled; configuration is applied through subcircuit parameters instead.
*
* Pins:
*   ADR AGND BST EN GOS MS1 MS2 PG PGND SCL SDA SW VCC VIN VOS_FB
*   (ADR/MS1/MS2/SCL/SDA are placeholders - leave open. GOS = remote
*   ground sense. VOS_FB = output voltage sense / feedback input.)
*
* User-settable parameters (defaults match the SIMPLIS release):
*   FSW=800k       switching frequency [Hz]: 500k, 600k, 800k, 1000k,
*                  1200k, 1400k
*   MODE=0         0 = FCCM, 1 = auto-skip Eco-mode (PFM)
*   OCL=21         valley current limit [A]. TPS544B2x: 4,7,10,13,15,18,21
*                  TPS544A2x: 4,7,10,13  (values above 13 clip to 13 in
*                  silicon; defaults: B=21, A=13)
*                  TPS544628: 4,5,6,7 (values above 7 clip to 7)
*   T_SS=1m        soft-start time [s]: 0.5m, 1m, 2m, 4m
*   VREF_CTRL=0.5  reference voltage [V]. Internal FB: VREF_CTRL=VOUT*VOSCL.
*                  External FB: VREF_CTRL per datasheet.
*   VOSCL=0.5      VOUT_SCALE_LOOP: 1, 0.5, 0.25, 0.125 (use 1 for
*                  external feedback)
*   INT_FB=1       1 = internal feedback divider (connect VOUT to VOS_FB),
*                  0 = external divider into VOS_FB
*   RAMP=2         COMP (D4h[2:0]) internal ramp selection, 0..7
*   D1H_BIT2=0     D1h command bit 2 (internal ripple LPF trim)
*   STEADY_STATE=0 1 = start pre-biased near regulation (fast settling,
*                  analogous to HAS_POP_ANALYSIS in the SIMPLIS release)
* Advanced (per-grade power stage; defaults = released 20A stage):
*   RON_HS=9m      high-side FET on-resistance
*   RON_LS=3.3m    low-side FET on-resistance
*   TPS544628=0    1 = TPS544628 (TPS544B2x_TRANS only): OCL<=7A, NOCL 3A,
*                  RON_HS/RON_LS fixed at 18m/7.5m (RON_* inputs ignored)
*
* Device-grade selection (top-level schematic parameters, one .OLB symbol):
*   TPS544B2x=1, TPS544A2x=0  -> 20A grade  (TPS544B28 / TPS544B26, OCL=21A)
*   TPS544B2x=0, TPS544A2x=1  -> 12A grade  (TPS544A28 / TPS544A26, OCL=13A)
*   TPS544628=1               -> TPS544628 (6A, OCL=7A), overrides the two flags above
*   Set exactly one flag to 1. Internally these flags drive
*   the OCL default seen by the TPS544X28_CORE subcircuit. The 28 (PMBus)
*   and 26 (I2C) suffixes are electrically identical in this model because
*   the digital interface is not modeled.
*
* Typical use (internal FB, VOUT=1V, 800kHz, 20A grade):
*   X1 ADR 0 BST EN GOS MS1 MS2 PG 0 SCL SDA SW VCC VIN VOUT TPS544B28
*   + PARAMS: FSW=800k VREF_CTRL=0.5 VOSCL=0.5 INT_FB=1 OCL=21 T_SS=1m
*   (tie VOS_FB to VOUT at the remote sense point; GOS to remote ground)
*
* Model Usage Notes:
*
* A. Features have been modeled
*   1.  Output voltage setting (internal or external feedback divider)
*   2.  Programmable soft start
*   3.  Switching-frequency and FCCM / auto-skip (Eco-mode) selection
*   4.  Low-side FET zero-crossing detection
*   5.  Current sense and positive overcurrent protection (grade-dependent)
*   6.  Low-side FET negative current limit
*   7.  Power good
*   8.  Output overvoltage protection (OVP)
*   9.  Output undervoltage protection (UVP)
*   10. EN/VIN UVLO protection
*   11. BOOT functionality
*   12. Pre-bias startup
*
* B. Features have not been modeled
*   1. Operating quiescent current
*   2. Shutdown current
*   3. Temperature-dependent characteristics
*   4. Hiccup / latch-off fault behavior
*   5. PMBus/I2C communication and telemetry (ADR/MS1/MS2/SCL/SDA are
*      placeholders; configuration is applied through subcircuit
*      parameters, not strap resistors or the digital bus)
*   6. Output voltage discharge
*   7. Multiphase operation and current sharing (single-phase buck only)
*
*******************************************************************************
**$ENCRYPTED_LIB
**$INTERFACE

